\ln\\left(p\\right)-1-\\ln\\left(3\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-b08edc19-ac2a-51a3-84d4-2578f86c837e" :answer/id #uuid "b08edc19-ac2a-51a3-84d4-2578f86c837e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\ln\\left(3\\right)-\\ln\\left(p\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-86b6ef8d-daaf-5ca0-8b6d-bbdd80985e9d" :answer/id #uuid "86b6ef8d-daaf-5ca0-8b6d-bbdd80985e9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln\\left(3\\right)-1-\\ln\\left(p\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-6cfc4395-e911-5b75-a1e7-1e707725c094" :answer/id #uuid "6cfc4395-e911-5b75-a1e7-1e707725c094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "answer-6ec80416-a1b1-58f9-91e7-aa443da3ba74" :answer/id #uuid "6ec80416-a1b1-58f9-91e7-aa443da3ba74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "field-3a977a92-4f32-521c-9aee-2d81d23948aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a977a92-4f32-521c-9aee-2d81d23948aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6760730-d6ae-5072-aa58-9d9b93a0503a" "answer-b08edc19-ac2a-51a3-84d4-2578f86c837e" "answer-86b6ef8d-daaf-5ca0-8b6d-bbdd80985e9d" "answer-6cfc4395-e911-5b75-a1e7-1e707725c094" "answer-6ec80416-a1b1-58f9-91e7-aa443da3ba74"] :answer-field/correct "answer-6ec80416-a1b1-58f9-91e7-aa443da3ba74" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "question-af4496a0-7154-51f1-8acd-df7c2bee4640" :question/id #uuid "af4496a0-7154-51f1-8acd-df7c2bee4640" :question/problem "Assume $p>0$.\n\n$\\ln\\left(\\frac{e\\cdot p}{3}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule for logarithms, separate the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(\\frac{e\\cdot p}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(e\\cdot p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use the product rule to expand the logarithm of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(e\\cdot p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(e\\right)+\\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\ln\\left(e\\right)=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(e\\right)+\\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right) \\\\ &=1+\\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["field-3a977a92-4f32-521c-9aee-2d81d23948aa"] :db/ensure :question/validate} [:db/add 17592186054624 :knowledge-point/questions "question-af4496a0-7154-51f1-8acd-df7c2bee4640"] [:db/cas 17592186608285 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186608296 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186608300 :question/retired nil true] [:db/cas 17592186608299 :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule and then the product rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln\\left(\\frac{q\\cdot 2}{e}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(q\\cdot 2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right) \\\\ &= -\\ln\\left(e\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)+\\ln\\left(q\\right) \\\\ &= -1+\\ln\\left(2\\right)+\\ln\\left(q\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\ln\\left(e\\right)=1$." "Using the quotient rule for logarithms, separate the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(\\frac{q\\cdot 2}{e}\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(q\\cdot 2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use the product rule to expand the logarithm of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(q\\cdot 2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(q\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\ln\\left(e\\right)=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(q\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(q\\right)+\\ln\\left(2\\right)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/ensure 17592186608299 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186608308 :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, combine the logarithms with the same sign. Then use the quotient rule to subtract the denominator logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log\\left(9\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) &= \\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Using the product rule for logarithms, combine the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\log\\left(9\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=\\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use the quotient rule to combine the remaining difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=\\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/ensure 17592186608308 :question/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186054624 :knowledge-point/validate]]
